## 2. Two Threads Running at the Same Time

This mirrors the weather/power file example from your lecture.

```java
public class TwoThreadsExample {

    // Thread 1 — pretends to process weather data
    static class WeatherThread extends Thread {
        @Override
        public void run() {
            System.out.println("WeatherThread: Starting to read weather file...");

            // Simulate the time it takes to read and process a file
            // Thread.sleep() pauses this thread for a given number of milliseconds
            // It's like the chef waiting for water to boil
            try {
                Thread.sleep(2000); // Pause for 2 seconds
            } catch (InterruptedException e) {
                e.printStackTrace();
            }

            System.out.println("WeatherThread: Done! Average temperature = 11.0°C");
        }
    }

    // Thread 2 — pretends to process power usage data
    static class PowerThread extends Thread {
        @Override
        public void run() {
            System.out.println("PowerThread: Starting to read power file...");

            try {
                Thread.sleep(3000); // This one takes a bit longer — 3 seconds
            } catch (InterruptedException e) {
                e.printStackTrace();
            }

            System.out.println("PowerThread: Done! Average power usage = 456.0 MWh");
        }
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        WeatherThread weatherThread = new WeatherThread();
        PowerThread powerThread = new PowerThread();

        // Both threads start almost simultaneously
        // They run in parallel — neither waits for the other
        weatherThread.start();
        powerThread.start();

        System.out.println("Main: Both threads have been started!");
        // Notice: this line prints BEFORE the threads finish
        // The main program doesn't automatically wait for them
    }
}

/* Expected output (order may vary slightly):
   Main: Both threads have been started!
   WeatherThread: Starting to read weather file...
   PowerThread: Starting to read power file...
   WeatherThread: Done! Average temperature = 11.0°C
   PowerThread: Done! Average power usage = 456.0 MWh
*/
```

